sequenceDiagram
    participant CP as CheckpointerMain
    participant CCF as CreateCheckPoint
    participant CPG as CheckPointGuts
    participant CPB as CheckPointBuffers
    participant BS as BufferSync
    participant SOB as SyncOneBuffer
    participant FB as FlushBuffer
    participant XL as XLogFlush
    participant SM as Storage Manager
    participant OS as Operating System

    Note over CP,OS: Checkpoint Buffer Flushing Sequence

    CP->>CCF: CreateCheckPoint(flags)
    CCF->>CPG: CheckPointGuts(checkPoint.redo, flags)
    CPG->>CPB: CheckPointBuffers(flags)
    CPB->>BS: BufferSync(flags)

    Note over BS: Phase 1: Buffer Pool Scan (Mark dirty buffers)
    loop For each buffer in shared_buffers
        BS->>BS: LockBufHdr(bufHdr)
        BS->>BS: Check (buf_state & BM_DIRTY && BM_PERMANENT)
        alt Buffer is dirty and needs checkpoint
            BS->>BS: buf_state |= BM_CHECKPOINT_NEEDED
            BS->>BS: Add to CkptBufferIds[num_to_scan++]
            Note right of BS: Store: buf_id, tsId, relNumber, forkNum, blockNum
        end
        BS->>BS: UnlockBufHdr(bufHdr, buf_state)
    end

    Note over BS: Phase 2: I/O Optimization
    BS->>BS: sort_checkpoint_bufferids(CkptBufferIds, num_to_scan)
    Note right of BS: Sort by: tablespace → relation → fork → block

    BS->>BS: Build per-tablespace statistics
    loop For each unique tablespace
        BS->>BS: Create CkptTsStatus entry
        BS->>BS: Calculate progress_slice = total_buffers / ts_buffers
    end

    BS->>BS: binaryheap_allocate(num_spaces, ts_ckpt_progress_comparator)
    BS->>BS: Initialize heap with tablespace progress tracking

    Note over BS: Phase 3: Balanced Buffer Writing
    loop While heap not empty
        BS->>BS: ts_stat = binaryheap_first(ts_heap)
        BS->>BS: buf_id = CkptBufferIds[ts_stat->index].buf_id

        BS->>SOB: SyncOneBuffer(buf_id, false, &wb_context)

        SOB->>SOB: bufHdr = GetBufferDescriptor(buf_id)
        SOB->>SOB: ReservePrivateRefCountEntry()
        SOB->>SOB: buf_state = LockBufHdr(bufHdr)

        alt Buffer still needs checkpoint
            SOB->>SOB: Check pg_atomic_read_u32(&bufHdr->state) & BM_CHECKPOINT_NEEDED

            alt Buffer is dirty and valid
                SOB->>SOB: PinBuffer_Locked(bufHdr)
                SOB->>SOB: LWLockAcquire(BufferDescriptorGetContentLock(bufHdr), LW_SHARED)

                SOB->>FB: FlushBuffer(bufHdr, NULL, IOOBJECT_RELATION, IOCONTEXT_NORMAL)

                FB->>FB: if (!StartBufferIO(buf, false, false)) return
                Note right of FB: Sets BM_IO_IN_PROGRESS, prevents concurrent writes

                FB->>FB: Setup error context callback
                FB->>FB: reln = smgropen(BufTagGetRelFileLocator(&buf->tag))

                FB->>FB: buf_state = LockBufHdr(buf)
                FB->>FB: recptr = BufferGetLSN(buf)
                FB->>FB: buf_state &= ~BM_JUST_DIRTIED
                FB->>FB: UnlockBufHdr(buf, buf_state)

                Note over FB,XL: WAL-Before-Data Rule Enforcement
                alt Permanent relation
                    FB->>XL: XLogFlush(recptr)
                    Note right of XL: Ensure WAL records hit disk first
                    XL-->>FB: WAL flushed to LSN
                end

                FB->>FB: bufBlock = BufHdrGetBlock(buf)
                FB->>FB: bufToWrite = PageSetChecksumCopy(bufBlock, blockNum)
                Note right of FB: Private copy allows concurrent hint bit updates

                FB->>FB: io_start = pgstat_prepare_io_time(track_io_timing)
                FB->>SM: smgrwrite(reln, forkNum, blockNum, bufToWrite, false)

                SM->>OS: Actual disk write operation
                OS-->>SM: Write completion status
                SM-->>FB: I/O operation complete

                FB->>FB: pgstat_count_io_op_time(IOOBJECT_RELATION, io_context, IOOP_WRITE, io_start, 1)
                FB->>FB: pgBufferUsage.shared_blks_written++

                FB->>FB: TerminateBufferIO(buf, true, 0, true)
                Note right of FB: Clear BM_IO_IN_PROGRESS, mark buffer clean

                FB-->>SOB: Buffer flushed successfully

                SOB->>SOB: LWLockRelease(BufferDescriptorGetContentLock(bufHdr))
                SOB->>SOB: tag = bufHdr->tag
                SOB->>SOB: UnpinBuffer(bufHdr)
                SOB->>SOB: ScheduleBufferTagForWriteback(wb_context, IOCONTEXT_NORMAL, &tag)

                SOB-->>BS: return BUF_WRITTEN

                BS->>BS: PendingCheckpointerStats.buffers_written++
                BS->>BS: num_written++
            else
                SOB->>SOB: UnlockBufHdr(bufHdr, buf_state)
                SOB-->>BS: return 0 (buffer not written)
            end
        else
            SOB-->>BS: return 0 (checkpoint flag cleared)
        end

        BS->>BS: ts_stat->progress += ts_stat->progress_slice
        BS->>BS: ts_stat->num_scanned++
        BS->>BS: ts_stat->index++

        alt All buffers from tablespace processed
            BS->>BS: binaryheap_remove_first(ts_heap)
        else
            BS->>BS: binaryheap_replace_first(ts_heap, PointerGetDatum(ts_stat))
        end

        Note over BS: I/O Throttling
        BS->>BS: CheckpointWriteDelay(flags, (double) num_processed / num_to_scan)
        Note right of BS: Sleep if ahead of checkpoint_completion_target schedule
    end

    Note over BS: Completion Phase
    BS->>BS: IssuePendingWritebacks(&wb_context, IOCONTEXT_NORMAL)
    Note right of BS: Batch flush hints to operating system

    BS->>BS: CheckpointStats.ckpt_bufs_written += num_written
    BS->>BS: pfree(per_ts_stat), binaryheap_free(ts_heap)

    BS-->>CPB: Buffer sync complete
    CPB-->>CPG: CheckPointBuffers complete

    Note over CPG: Continue with other checkpoint operations
    CPG->>CPG: ProcessSyncRequests() - fsync all pending requests

    CPG-->>CCF: CheckPointGuts complete
    CCF-->>CP: CreateCheckPoint complete

    Note over CP,OS: Key Optimizations Highlighted
    Note over BS: 1. Tablespace-balanced I/O prevents hotspots
    Note over FB: 2. WAL-before-data ensures consistency
    Note over SOB: 3. Writeback hints optimize OS scheduling
    Note over BS: 4. Adaptive throttling spreads I/O load